{"signature": "{\"text\": \"Energy cannot be created or destroyed. It can be transferred between stores by mechanical work, electrical work, heating or radiation. In a closed system, no energy is transferred into or out of the system, so the total energy remains constant. Be careful: in thermodynamics, a closed system may exchange energy but not matter with its surroundings. For GCSE energy-conservation questions, the important condition is that no energy crosses the boundary of the system when we claim its total energy stays constant; this is more precisely an isolated system.\", \"voice\": \"en-NG-AbeoNeural\", \"rate\": \"-4%\", \"eleven\": true}", "duration": 36.806531, "words": [["Energy", 0.0], ["cannot", 0.464], ["be", 0.766], ["created", 0.894], ["or", 1.474], ["destroyed.", 1.649], ["It", 2.368], ["can", 2.601], ["be", 2.856], ["transferred", 2.984], ["between", 3.541], ["stores", 3.947], ["by", 4.47], ["mechanical", 4.656], ["work,", 5.259], ["electrical", 5.759], ["work,", 6.444], ["heating", 7.001], ["or", 7.465], ["radiation.", 7.674], ["In", 8.661], ["a", 8.882], ["closed", 8.986], ["system,", 9.381], ["no", 10.17], ["energy", 10.484], ["is", 10.995], ["transferred", 11.122], ["into", 11.738], ["or", 12.214], ["out", 12.411], ["of", 12.701], ["the", 12.829], ["system,", 12.957], ["so", 13.642], ["the", 13.862], ["total", 14.013], ["energy", 14.454], ["remains", 14.942], ["constant.", 15.407], ["Be", 16.138], ["careful:", 16.394], ["in", 17.09], ["thermodynamics,", 17.287], ["a", 18.321], ["closed", 18.483], ["system", 18.843], ["may", 19.296], ["exchange", 19.54], ["energy", 20.144], ["but", 20.654], ["not", 20.887], ["matter", 21.142], ["with", 21.583], ["its", 21.815], ["surroundings.", 21.99], ["For", 22.93], ["GCSE", 23.151], ["energy-conservation", 23.975], ["questions,", 25.182], ["the", 25.96], ["important", 26.123], ["condition", 26.634], ["is", 27.202], ["that", 27.411], ["no", 27.69], ["energy", 27.969], ["crosses", 28.421], ["the", 28.874], 